00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.190
make that call.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.320
Like, I thought she was sober enough.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.171
I mean, that was my, kind
of, my job was to decide...

00:07:12.171 --> 00:07:13.470
- [Kelly] And you want to
believe in your parent,

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.640
you wanna believe in that right?

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:15.473
- [Andie MacDowell] It wasn't even that.

00:07:15.473 --> 00:07:16.306
I mean, no.

00:07:16.306 --> 00:07:17.139
- [Kelly] No?

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:18.900
- No, I mean, I, I really was
taking care of her, honestly.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.720
I mean, it was me trying
to figure out if she was

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.550
sober enough, and I felt really guilty...

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.947
- That's a lot on a kid.

00:07:24.947 --> 00:07:25.873
- [Andie MacDowell] A lot, it's a lot.

00:07:25.873 --> 00:07:26.706
- Yeah.

00:07:26.706 --> 00:07:27.539
- [Andie MacDowell] It's a lot to say,

00:07:27.539 --> 00:07:28.372
"Oh, maybe you should call in."

00:07:28.372 --> 00:07:29.205
I just didn't think of it.

00:07:29.205 --> 00:07:30.270
Anyway, she got fired.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.880
And I asked for them to
give her her job back.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.860
But they didn't, so I quit.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:35.693
Which was...

00:07:35.693 --> 00:07:36.526
- [Kelly] solidarity. - Yeah.

00:07:36.526 --> 00:07:37.988
- You were like, "Well,
then I'm going too."

00:07:37.988 --> 00:07:38.821
- Yeah, what could I do?

00:07:38.821 --> 00:07:40.500
Wasn't going to stay after they fired her.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.333
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:42.166
- So,...

00:07:42.166 --> 00:07:42.999
- I think what's interesting too,

00:07:42.999 --> 00:07:45.360
is when I have, like, my
own abandonment issues,

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.200
like things going in my life....

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.180
But I think what's interesting
is how you perceive it

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.467
as a child, and how you accept things,

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:52.530
and you don't know it was
kind of wrong, or not cool.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.390
And then you have kids,

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.507
and you go,...

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:58.440
"How in the world could
you walk away from a child?

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.230
How in the world could you
not want to be involved?"

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.940
It's an interesting thing to have kids,

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.550
and have a completely
different perspective on your

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:06.929
childhood, because of their childhood.

00:08:06.929 --> 00:08:07.762
- [Andie MacDowell] Mhmmm.

00:08:07.762 --> 00:08:08.595
- [Kelly] You know what
I'm saying? - Mhmmm.

00:08:08.595 --> 00:08:09.428
- [Kelly] And then it's kind of cool too,

00:08:09.428 --> 00:08:11.700
because it's like, all
right, I know what not to do.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.800
I know it didn't work, at
least for me when I was a kid.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.270
So, I'm gonna try, and do better.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:18.990
- I know I got a lot of things
better than what I received,

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.510
because I was able to make improvements.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.000
But I talked to my kids about
making their own improvements,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.833
because...

00:08:24.833 --> 00:08:25.690
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.700
- I don't feel like I
got everything, for sure.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.533
- [Kelly] And no one does.

00:08:27.533 --> 00:08:28.500
If you're saying so, you're a liar.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.333
- Yeah. - So,...

00:08:29.333 --> 00:08:33.300
- But I think I made vast
improvements on what I,

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.590
my experience was.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.990
But also, it's such a different time,

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.520
because we talk about all this now.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.470
And this was not anything that was ever...

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:42.690
We didn't speak about
these kinds of things.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:43.523
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.356
- And, um,...

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.770
You know, my mother had shock
treatments after I was born.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.860
She, she had what they would've
called a nervous breakdown.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:52.170
It could have been partially postpartum.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.180
So many things that it could have been.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.880
And she was diagnosed with
schizophrenia, so she,

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.430
you know, she was, had a lot of trouble.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.263
- Yeah.

00:09:00.263 --> 00:09:01.096
- [Andie MacDowell] And it,...

00:09:01.096 --> 00:09:02.340
was not able to get the
care that she needed to get,

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.450
because of the time.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:04.740
- [Kelly] Which is why
it's so important now

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.900
that we're talking about stuff like this,

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.110
so people have access,

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.157
and opportunity to care.

00:09:08.157 --> 00:09:10.110
- [Andie MacDowell] So, so, so important.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.680
But anyway, to get back to
my, to my beautiful children,

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.470
I did, I took this course on parenting.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.328
And one of the...

00:09:17.328 --> 00:09:18.161
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:09:18.161 --> 00:09:18.994
- [Andie MacDowell] Yeah, yeah.

00:09:18.994 --> 00:09:20.670
And one of the things
they taught us, like,

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:22.597
they asked like people in
the audience who were saying,

00:09:22.597 --> 00:09:24.360
"What do you think is the
most important thing you do

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.193
for your child?"

00:09:25.193 --> 00:09:28.770
And they were like, "Oh,
to make them be empathetic,

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.210
to want to give back to their community."

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.620
And all these beautiful things...

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.000
And, and he was like, "Yes,

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.470
all these things are really beautiful,

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.780
but what the most important
thing that you can

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:39.390
give your child is to
make them independent,

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.710
so they can fly."

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:41.543
You know?

00:09:41.543 --> 00:09:42.376
- Yeah.

00:09:42.376 --> 00:09:43.209
- It's like, "Oh, well that makes sense."

00:09:43.209 --> 00:09:44.042
Is to make them inde...

00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:45.180
Mine have flown away.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.430
- [Kelly] Yeah? - Mine flew away.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.870
- You've done a great job then.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.340
That's why I'm not a helicopter mom.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.459
I'm very independent with them.

00:09:51.459 --> 00:09:52.292
- [Andie MacDowell] Yes.

00:09:52.292 --> 00:09:53.580
- Like, I, I think I was raised like that.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.510
So I think that's important.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:55.343
- [Andie MacDowell] Yeah.

00:09:55.343 --> 00:09:56.820
- Because then by the time
they're, they are flying away

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.910
you feel like they're, you
know, prepared for that.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.151
- [Andie MacDowell] Yeah.

00:10:00.151 --> 00:10:00.984
- It's scary.

00:10:00.984 --> 00:10:02.010
- [Andie MacDowell] Mine
definitely flew the coop.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:02.843
- [Kelly] Yeah? - Yeah, they...

00:10:02.843 --> 00:10:03.763
- [Kelly] So you nailed it, way to go.

00:10:03.763 --> 00:10:04.950
- I know.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.232
- Killed it! - I know.

00:10:06.232 --> 00:10:07.065
(distant audience applauding)

